25::
0 :
Motion
1 :
Serious motion error\n
Not possible to proceed motion control\n
\t\n
Start up the system again
21 :
Joint position error\n
Actual position of joint %s\n
is too far away from the ordered\n
position\n
\t\n
Check trim parameters, external\n
forces or hardware.
22 :
Too low DC-link voltage\n
\t\n
Check voltage from Motor On contactors\n
Replace DC-link
23 :
Stop-/Restart error\n
The stop was made when too many move\n
instructions were queued for execution.\n
Restart is not possible\n
\t\n
Check the number of move instructions\n
with concurrency. Move the start point\n
and start a new movement.
24 :
Corner path failure\n
A corner path was executed as\n
a stop point due to a time delay.\n
\t\n
Check the number of instructions\n
between the move instructions.
25 :
Restart too far from path\n
\t\n
Move back to path.
26 :
Singularity or Zone error\n
1 Robot too close to singularity\n
2 MoveL to MoveJ corner zone error\n
\t\n
1 Use the joystick to move away from\n
  the singularity or run a program in\n
  joint coordinates\n
2 Use fine point or modify position
27 :
Joint Out of Range\n
Joint %s is out of working range\n
\t\n
Use the joystick to move the joint into\n
its working range
28 :
Jog in wrong direction\n
Joint %s is out of working range\n
\t\n
Use the joystick to move the joint in\n
opposite direction.
29 :
Robot outside its limits\n
The robot has reached the configuration\n
limit for the parallelogram transmission.\n
\t\n
Use the joystick to move the involved\n
joint into the working range again. 
30 :
Robot outside its limits\n
Jogging was made in wrong direction when\n
parallelogram was out of working range\n
\t\n
Use the joystick to move the joint in\n
opposite direction.
31 :
Command not allowed.\n
System parameters cannot be\n
changed in MOTORS ON state.\n
\t\n
Change to MOTORS OFF.
32 :
Calibration command error\n
An attempt was made to calibrate while\n
in MOTORS ON state.\n
\t\n
Change to MOTORS OFF.
33 :
Commutation command error\n
An attempt was made to commutate the\n
motors in MOTORS ON state.\n
\t\n
Change to MOTORS OFF.
35 :
Synchronization error\n
An attempt was made to synchronize\n
in MOTORS ON state.\n
\t\n
Change to MOTORS OFF.
36 :
Correct regain impossible\n
Correct regain impossible. A stop\n
occurred with too many close points\n
with corner zones. At restart the robot\n
will move to a point farther forward in\n
the program.\n
\t\n
Reduce the number of close points,\n
increase the distance between them or\n
reduce the speed.
37 :
MOTORS ON order ignored\n
MOTORS ON order ignored since the\n
previous stop was not yet acknowledged.\n
\t\n
Order MOTORS ON again.
41 :
Robot in a singularity\n
The Robot is too close to a singularity.\n
\t\n
During program execution, use SingArea\n
instruction or joint interpolation.\n
During jogging, use axis by axis.
42 :
System error\n
\t\n
Increase the distance between close\n
points and/or decrease speed and/or\n
change acceleration value.
50 :
Position outside reach\n
Position for IRB joint %.f\n
is outside working area.\n
\t\n
Check the work object.\n
Check the joint working range.\n
Move the joint in joint coordinates.
52 :
Joint speed error\n
The speed of joint %s is too high\n
relative the ordered speed\n
\t\n
1. Check the tune parameters, external\n
   forces on the joint and hardware.\n
2. Reduce programmed speed.
53 :
Revolution counter error\n
Too big difference between the counter\n
in the serial measurement board and\n
the expected value in the robot computer\n
for joint %s\n
\t\n
Update the revolution counter\n
Replace serial measurement board
55 :
Joint load error\n
Actual torque on joint %s is\n
higher than ordered.\n
\t\n
May be caused by incorrect load data,\n
hardware error or to high acceleration.\n
1. Check load data\n
2. Check hardware\n
3. Reduce acceleration
56 :
Joint collision error\n
Actual torque on joint %s is\n
higher than ordered while at low\n
or zero speed.\n
\t\n
May be caused by jam error (the arm\n
has got stuck) or hardware error.
57 :
Joint sync. error\n
The position of joint %s after\n
power failure is too far away from the\n
position before the power failure.\n
\t\n
Make a new update of the revo-\n
lution counter.
58 :
Tool coord. sys. error\n
The z-direction of the tool coordinate\n
system is almost parallel with the path\n
direction.\n
\t\n
Change the tool coordinate system to\n
achieve at least 3 degrees deviation \n
between z-direction and path direction.
59 :
Frame error\n
The definition of robot\n
fixed tool is not correct.\n
\t\n
Check the tool and object data.
60 :
Frame error\n
The definition of robot\n
fixed tool is not correct.\n
\t\n
Check the tool and object data.
61 :
Frame error\n
The definition of robot\n
fixed tool is not correct.\n
\t\n
Check the tool and object data.
62 :
Circle programming error\n
Start and end positions for the circle\n
are too close.\n
\t
63 :
Circle programming error\n
The circle position is too close to the\n
start or end position of the circle.\n
\t
65 :
Kinematics error\n
The destination of the movement is\n
outside the reach of the robot or too\n
close to a singularity.\n
\t\n
Change the destination position.
66 :
Robot not active\n
Attempt to coordinate motion or\n
calculate position of deactivated\n
robot %s.\n
\t\n
Activate robot via the Motion Unit key,\n
then Jogging window, or program.\n
Check work object and program.
67 :
Unit not active\n
Attempt to coordinate motion or\n
calculate position of deactivated\n
single unit %s.\n
\t\n
Activate unit via Motion Unit key,\n
then Jogging window, or program.\n
Check work object and program.
76 :
Orientation def. error\n
Orientation is incorrectly defined.\n
\t\n
Make an accurate normalization of\n
the quaternion elements.
78 :
Too many close positions\n
Too many consecutive closely spaced\n
positions.\n
\t\n
Increase the distance between\n
consecutive close positions.
79 :
Wrist weaving not possible.\n
\t\n
Use smaller weaving amplitude or a\n
larger TCP.
80 :
Position not compatible.\n
Position cannot be reached with the\n
given robot configuration\n
\t\n
Modify the robot position\n
in the program.
82 :
Deceleration limit\n
Calculation of joint deceleration time\n
exceeds internal limits for this motion\n
\n
Do not proceed without removing the\n
causes of the error. See Check\n
\t\n
Check deceleration of external axes.\n
Check noise level on I/O connections.\n
Increase Path resolution, Queue length.\n
Decrease program speed, and/or increase\n
AccSet parameters (if below 100%).
83 :
Speed lowered by system.\n
The speed has been lowered by the system\n
due to dynamic limitations.\n
\t\n
Decrease speed and/or do not use close\n
positions at high speed and/or increase\n
acceleration (if below 100%).
85 :
Too many user frames.\n
For mech_unit %s more than one\n
user frame has been defined.\n
\t\n
Take away one user frame or define\n
one more mech_unit.
86 :
Singularity calc. error\n
Too close to wrist singularity with\n
respect to numerical resolution\n
for joint 4 of IRB.\n
\t\n
Change destination position a few\n
increments.
87 :
Singularity problems.\n
Too close to wrist singularity with\n
respect to numerical resolution\n
for joint 6 of IRB.\n
\t\n
Change destination position a few\n
increments.
88 :
Restart not possible.\n
It is not possible to restart the path\n
due to a previous error.\n
\t\n
Move the program start point and start\n
a new movement.
89 :
Lower weaving frequency\n
The weaving period length or\n
period time is too short.\n
\t\n
Increase weave length or \n
increase period time.
91 :
Restart not possible.\n
Restart no longer possible. Change of\n
unit state made restart of program\n
impossible.\n
\t\n
Move the program pointer and start\n
a new movement.
92 :
Axis computer comm. error\n
Incorrect response from axis computer\n
\t\n
Check motion configuration parameters.\n
Check axis computer hardware.
93 :
Load too large\n
The defined load mass is too large
94 :
ServoTune not possible.\n
Tuning is not implemented for the\n
specified Joint.\n
\t
95 :
Cannot access joint.\n
Cannot access external joint. Check\n
configuration and activation of\n
external Joints.\n
\t
100 :
Manipulator error\n
There are more configuration or\n
numerical errors in motion domain.\n
\t\n
Correct previous ones and try again.
101 :
Manipulator config. error\n
'%s' is  not free\n
for the param. '%s'\n
in type '%s' named\n
'%s'.\n
\t\n
Use another one.\n
For internal names, see moc_chk.log.
102 :
Manipulator config. error\n
'%s' used in the\n
parameter '%s' in\n
type '%s' named\n
'%s' is not\n
defined.\n
\t\n
Use another one that is defined or\n
define the used one.\n
For internal names, see moc_chk.log.
103 :
Num. error in manipulator\n
The orientation defined by quaternions\n
including '%s' in\n
the type '%s' named\n
'%s' is not\n
normalized.(SQRSUM =1)\n
\t\n
Check the quaternions and/or recalculate\n
them.\n
For internal names, see moc_chk.log.
104 :
Num. error in manipulator\n
The parameter '%s'\n
in type '%s' named\n
'%s' is not '%s'.\n
\t\n
Check the value.\n
For internal names, see moc_chk.log.
128 :
Manipulator error\n
Terminating the topic check for\n 
manipulator due to earlier errors.\n
\t\n
Correct the reported errors and run\n
topic check again.
130 :
Synchronization failed.\n
Synchronization failed for joint\n
%s.\n
\t\n
Make a new synchronization.\n
Restart System.
131 :
Calibration failed.\n
Calibration failed for joint\n
%s.\n
\t\n
Make a new calibration.\n
Restart System.
132 :
Commutation failed.\n
Commutation failed for joint\n
%s.\n
\t\n
Make a new commutation.\n
Restart System.
133 :
Test signal error.\n
No test signals are available\n
for the master robot.\n
\t
134 :
Corr. vector warning\n
Sensor correction vector calculations\n
failed due to previous error.\n
\t
135 :
SoftAct not possible.\n
Soft servo is not possible to activate.\n
\t
136 :
SoftAct not possible.\n
Soft servo is not possible to modify.\n
during ramping.\n
\t
137 :
Fine point inserted\n
Corner zone is changed to fine point\n
Too many consecutive Move instructions\n
without fine point\n
\t
138 :
Arm check point outside\n
The robot has reached the limit for arm\n
check point\n
\t\n
Use the joystick to move the involved\n
joint into the working range again
139 :
Arm check point outside\n
Jogging was made in wrong direction when\n
arm check point was out of working range\n
\t\n
Use the joystick to move the joint in\n
opposite direction.
140 :
Payload too large\n
Heavy payload caused static torque\n
limit to be exceeded on joint %s\n
\t\n
Check and reduce payload\n
for arm and/or wrist.\n
Reduce joint working range to decrease\n
static torque due to gravity.
141 :
Speed, Zone or Jog error\n
1. Robot too close to singularity\n
2. MoveL to MoveJ corner zone error\n
3. Jogging error\n
4. High speed error\n
\t\n
1. Move away from the singularity or run\n
   the program in joint coordinates\n
2. Use fine point or modify position\n
3. Try again\n
4. Reduce the programmed speed
142 :
Manipulator config. error\n
Configuration of the manipulator failed.\n
\t\n
Check the parameter values under\n
System parameters:Manipultor.
143 :
Robot axes config. error\n
Actual configuration is not the same\n
as commanded configuration.\n
\t\n
Use SingArea_Wrist or ConfL_Off\n
or modify position
144 :
Displ frame uncertain.\n
Calibration of displ frame uncertain\n
1. Wrong TCP\n
2. Ref. points inaccurate\n
3. Ref. points badly spaced\n
\t\n
If estimated error is unacceptable:\n
1. Verify that correct TCP is used.\n
2. Try more than 3 ref. points.\n
3. Be careful when positioning robot\n
   to ref. points.
145 :
Kinematic limitation.\n
No solution obtained, possibly because\n
of long segment or robot in a configura-\n
tion with bad motion condition\n
\t\n
Insert an intermediary point to reduce\n
the length of the segment.
146 :
Restart limitation\n
Corner path executed as a stop point.\n
Power fail restart not possible near\n
the stop point.\n
\t\n
Use finepoint in the Move-instr before\n
RestoPath, ActUnit, Wait or Stop-instr\n
to make power fail restart possible.
147 :
Power fail restart failed\n
Re-creation of the path failed\n
\t\n
Move the start point and start\n
a new movement.
148 :
MOC_WRONG_MAIN_ISR_TYPE\n
Error when trying to call a non existing\n
interrupt routine in the main computer\n
from the axis computer.\n
\t
149 :
MOC_SCHED_QUEUE_FULL\n
Error when the scheduler queue in the\n
axis computer is full.\n
\t
150 :
MOC_WRONG_CMD_TYPE\n
Error when the axis computer have\n
received a command from the main\n
computer that is not supported.\n
\t
151 :
MOC_MAILBOX1_ERROR\n
The axis computer driver failed\n
to generate a new mailbox 1 interrupt\n
since the previous interrupt has\n
not been serviced properly.\n
\t
152 :
MOC_MAILBOX2_ERROR\n
The axis computer driver failed\n
to generate a new mailbox 2 interrupt\n
since the previous interrupt has\n
not been serviced properly.\n
\t
153 :
Command not allowed\n
The given instruction, or command, was\n
not allowed since the robot program was\n 
executing in a hold state.\n
\t\n
Modify program or stop program execution\n
before issuing command.
155 :
Power fail restart failed\n
Not possible to restart the Move-instr\n
before RestoPath, ActUnit, Wait or\n
Stop-instr\n
\t\n
Make program free from MOTION WARNING\n
50146 Restart limitation, by changing\n
the Move-instr to finepoint\n
Move the start point and start\n
a new movement.\n

